  "title": "Angles formed by parallel lines and a transversal",
  "summary": "Use corresponding, alternate and co-interior angle relationships.",
  "outcomes": [
    "1.3"
  ],
  "prerequisite_lessons": [
    "g1-lesson-02"
  ],
  "estimated_minutes": 55,
  "objectives": [
    "Recognise corresponding, alternate and co-interior angle relationships.",
    "Calculate unknown angles formed by parallel lines and a transversal.",
    "Use angle relationships to justify when two lines are parallel."
  ],
  "mastery_policy_key": "g1-default-v1",
  "sections": [
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-13-method",
      "position": 1,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Recognising the F, Z and C relationships",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For parallel lines, corresponding angles are equal, alternate interior angles are equal, and co-interior angles (also called same-side interior angles) on the same side of a transversal total 180°."
        },
        {
          "type": "display_math",
          "latex": "\\text{corresponding}=\\text{equal},\\quad\\text{alternate}=\\text{equal},\\quad\\text{co-interior sum}=180^\\circ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-03-visual",
      "position": 2,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Read the diagram",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The diagram shows two parallel lines, marked with arrows, cut by a transversal. The 68° angle at the upper line and the angle x at the lower line are in the same position at each crossing, so they are corresponding angles. The arrow marks, not the appearance of the lines, tell you that the lines are parallel."
        },
        {
          "type": "asset_ref",
          "asset_key": "g1-lesson-03-diagram"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-03-reasoning",
      "position": 3,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Reasoning method",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Trace a Z shape for alternate angles, an F shape for corresponding angles and a C shape for co-interior angles, but always confirm which lines form the angle. Converse facts also work: if a valid pair of corresponding or alternate angles is equal, or co-interior angles total 180°, the lines are parallel."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-13-example",
      "position": 4,
      "type": "worked_example",
      "title": "Worked example: corresponding angles",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the diagram, two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. Find x."
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The 68° angle and x are in the same position at the two crossings, above each line and to the right of the transversal. They form an F shape, so they are corresponding angles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The lines are parallel, so corresponding angles are equal."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "x=68^\\circ"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "verification_note": "Check with a second fact: the angle just below 68° on the upper line is 180° − 68° = 112°, and it is co-interior with x, so 112° + 68° should be 180°. It is."
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-03-example-2",
      "position": 5,
      "type": "worked_example",
      "title": "Worked example: co-interior expressions",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. A co-interior pair is (3x + 12)° and (5x − 8)°. Find x and both angles."
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Co-interior angles between parallel lines are supplementary."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "(3x+12)+(5x-8)=180"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "8x+4=180\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=22"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "position": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The angles are 3(22) + 12 = 78° and 5(22) − 8 = 102°."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "verification_note": "The calculated angles add to 180°, as a co-interior pair must."
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-03-pitfalls",
      "position": 6,
      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Common errors and checks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Do not use a parallel-line fact unless parallel arrows are shown or parallelism has been proved. Corresponding and alternate angles are equal; co-interior angles are supplementary. Keep the transversal fixed when identifying the pair."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-13-recall",
      "position": 7,
      "type": "active_recall",
      "title": "Check your understanding",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. One angle of a co-interior pair is 117°. Find the other angle, in degrees."
        }
      ],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "comparison_mode": "exact_numeric",
        "canonical_answer": "63",
        "canonical_latex": "63",
        "accepted_answers": [],
        "absolute_tolerance": null,
        "rounding_precision": null,
        "unit": null
      },
      "feedback": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Co-interior angles between parallel lines total 180°, so 180 − 117 = 63."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stable_key": "g1-lesson-03-summary",
      "position": 8,
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Method checklist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "With parallel lines: corresponding angles (F) are equal, alternate angles (Z) are equal, and co-interior angles (C) total 180°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use these facts only when the lines are marked or stated as parallel, and keep track of which transversal makes each angle."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
